      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The ground staff must immediately treat any suspected tampering or compromised seal as a critical event, activating the \"Red Alert\" protocol. First, they should isolate the specific container and the entire immediate vicinity, ensuring no unauthorized personnel approach, as even a single uninvited footstep can be a sign of a stealthy intrusion. If the seal is broken or the temperature data loggers show a spike, the shipment must be quarantined immediately; under no circumstances should the vaccine be moved to a new holding area without a full forensic audit.\n\nFor verification, the team must retrieve the data logger to analyze the temperature curve for the specific breach window. If the temperature excursion was brief and the product was kept at the correct temperature immediately after the breach, a third-party laboratory may perform a rapid stability test. However, if the temperature dropped below the safe threshold or if the breach was prolonged, the product must be declared non-compliant and destroyed to prevent any risk of infection, as a compromised chain is a direct threat to patient safety.\n\nIn the event of external interference, security teams should document all evidence, including photos of the broken seal and any suspicious items found, and report the incident to the local authorities and the central command. They should also",
